A path's leaf is recognised by its address alone. Once the leaf is freed
and its memory reused for another node at that address, the path is
replayed into that node, and an insert goes where the old leaf's position
said (#754).
Guarded-by: "blind tree: a path whose leaf was freed and its memory reused is not replayed"

diff --git a/bytecaskdb/blind_btree.cppm b/bytecaskdb/blind_btree.cppm
index a7d70663..ffae28b2 100644
--- a/bytecaskdb/blind_btree.cppm
+++ b/bytecaskdb/blind_btree.cppm
@@ -1513,7 +1513,7 @@ public:
     if (!cur->is_leaf)
       return Route::kKey;
     const auto at = node_address(cur);
-    if (at == p.leaf && cur->tag == p.leaf_tag)
+    if (at == p.leaf)
       return Route::kSame;
     if (at == f.now && f.write == writes_)
       return Route::kFollowed;
